ific group."}}, "reasoning_process": "Analyzing documents for: What is the name of the group of black Indians associated with the Seminole people?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-19T20:10:30.179361", "agent_role": "Analysis-Answer", "input_data": {"sub_question": "Where did the descendants of Black Seminoles settle?", "num_documents": 3}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"yes\",\n  \"answer\": \"The descendants of Black Seminoles settled in Florida, Oklahoma, and Coahuila, Mexico. Historically, they lived in distinct bands near the Seminole people in Florida, but some escaped slavery and settled in Coahuila, Mexico, forming the Mascogo community. Additionally, many Black Seminoles were forcibly relocated to Indian Territory (now Oklahoma) during the Second Seminole War, where their descendants are part of the Seminole Nation of Oklahoma.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The documents explicitly mention that Black Seminoles allied with Seminole groups in Spanish Florida and some escaped to Mexico, forming the Mascogo community in Coahuila. They also state that the Seminole Nation of Oklahoma includes descendants of Black Seminoles relocated from Florida. This provides sufficient information to answer the question.\"\n}", "parsed_result": {"status": "yes", "answer": "The descendants of Black Seminoles settled in Florida, Oklahoma, and Coahuila, Mexico. Historically, they lived in distinct bands near the Seminole people in Florida, but some escaped slavery and settled in Coahuila, Mexico, forming the Mascogo community. Additionally, many Black Seminoles were forcibly relocated to Indian Territory (now Oklahoma) during the Second Seminole War, where their descendants are part of the Seminole Nation of Oklahoma.", "analysis": "The documents explicitly mention that Black Seminoles allied with Seminole groups in Spanish Florida and some escaped to Mexico, forming the Mascogo community in Coahuila. They also state that the Seminole 