{"id": "5ab6c63755429953192ad38b", "question": "Siegfriedstellung in the First World War was a defensive position of what country's army?", "answer": "Germany", "gold_answer": "German", "wallclock_seconds": 38.3333, "trajectory": {"question": "Siegfriedstellung in the First World War was a defensive position of what country's army?", "strategic_plan": {"reasoning": "Strategic decomposition completed", "sub_questions": [{"step_id": 1, "sub_question": "What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "goal": "Collect information for: What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "dependencies": [], "expected_info_type": "general"}, {"step_id": 2, "sub_question": "Which country's army used [entity from step 1] as a defensive position?", "goal": "Collect information for: Which country's army used [entity from step 1] as a defensive position?", "dependencies": [1], "expected_info_type": "general"}]}, "execution_traces": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-19T22:21:26.617238", "agent_role": "PLAN", "input_data": {"question": "Siegfriedstellung in the First World War was a defensive position of what country's army?"}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"subgoal_id\": 1,\n    \"subgoal\": \"What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?\",\n    \"dependencies\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"subgoal_id\": 2, \n    \"subgoal\": \"Which country's army used [entity from step 1] as a defensive position?\",\n    \"dependencies\": [1]\n  }\n]", "parsed_plan": {"reasoning": "Strategic decomposition completed", "sub_questions": [{"step_id": 1, "sub_question": "What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "goal": "Collect information for: What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "dependencies": [], "expected_info_type": "general"}, {"step_id": 2, "sub_question": "Which country's army used [entity from step 1] as a defensive position?", "goal": "Collect information for: Which country's army used [entity from step 1] as a defensive position?", "dependencies": [1], "expected_info_type": "general"}]}}, "reasoning_process": "Decomposing complex question into sub-questions", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-19T22:21:40.507950", "agent_role": "Analysis-Answer", "input_data": {"sub_question": "What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "num_documents": 5}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"yes\",\n  \"answer\": \"The Siegfriedstellung, also known as the Hindenburg Line, was a German defensive position constructed during World War I on the Western Front from 1916 to 1917. It was part of the larger Hindenburg Line system, stretching over 630 km across northern France and Belgium. The line featured extensive fortifications, bunkers, tunnels, and tank traps, designed to provide a strong defensive barrier for the German army. It was built to allow a strategic withdrawal from the Somme front and counter anticipated Anglo-French offensives in 1917.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The documents explicitly define the Siegfriedstellung as the original name for the Hindenburg Line, detailing its construction period (1916\u20131917), location on the Western Front, and purpose as a defensive structure. Key details about its scale, fortifications, and strategic role in World War I are provided in chunks 317 and 318, confirming sufficient information to answer the question.\"\n}", "parsed_result": {"status": "yes", "answer": "The Siegfriedstellung, also known as the Hindenburg Line, was a German defensive position constructed during World War I on the Western Front from 1916 to 1917. It was part of the larger Hindenburg Line system, stretching over 630 km across northern France and Belgium. The line featured extensive fortifications, bunkers, tunnels, and tank traps, designed to provide a strong defensive barrier for the German army. It was built to allow a strategic withdrawal from the Somme front and counter anticipated Anglo-French offensives in 1917.", "analysis": "The documents explicitly define the Siegfriedstellung as the original name for the Hindenburg Line, detailing its construction period (1916\u20131917), location on the Western Front, and purpose as a defensive structure. Key details about its scale, fortifications, and strategic role in World War I are provided in chunks 317 and 318, confirming sufficient information to answer the question."}}, "reasoning_process": "Analyzing documents for: What was the Siegfriedstellung in the First World War?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-19T22:21:53.051916", "agent_role": "Analysis-Answer", "input_data": {"sub_question": "Which country's army used The Siegfriedstellung, also known as the Hindenburg Line, was a German defensive position constructed during World War I on the Western Front from 1916 to 1917. It was part of the larger Hindenburg Line system, stretching over 630 km across northern France and Belgium. The line featured extensive fortifications, bunkers, tunnels, and tank traps, designed to provide a strong defensive barrier for the German army. It was built to allow a strategic withdrawal from the Somme front and counter anticipated Anglo-French offensives in 1917. as a defensive position?", "num_documents": 3}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"yes\",\n  \"answer\": \"Germany\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The retrieved documents explicitly state that the Hindenburg Line (Siegfriedstellung) was a 'German defensive position of World War I' constructed on the Western Front. Multiple chunks (e.g., chunk_318, chunk_317) confirm its creation by Germany during 1916\u20131917 to support strategic withdrawals and counter Allied offensives. No conflicting information is present.\"\n}", "parsed_result": {"status": "yes", "answer": "Germany", "analysis": "The retrieved documents explicitly state that the Hindenburg Line (Siegfriedstellung) was a 'German defensive position of World War I' constructed on the Western Front. Multiple chunks (e.g., chunk_318, chunk_317) confirm its creation by Germany during 1916\u20131917 to support strategic withdrawals and counter Allied offensives. No conflicting information is present."}}, "reasoning_process": "Analyzing documents for: Which country's army used The Siegfriedstellung, also known as the Hindenburg Line, was a German defensive position constructed during World War I on the Western Front from 1916 to 1917. It was part of the larger Hindenburg Line system, stretching over 630 km across northern France and Belgium. The line featured extensive fortifications, bunkers, tunnels, and tank traps, designed to provide a strong defensive barrier for the German army. It was built to allow a strategic withdrawal from the Somme front and counter anticipated Anglo-French offensives in 1917. as a defensive position?", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}], "final_answer": "Germany", "total_time": 38.33302021026611, "retrieval_rounds": 2}, "question_id": "5ab6c63755429953192ad38b", "prompt_tokens": 10061, "completion_tokens": 1437, "total_tokens": 11498, "llm_call_count": 3, "total_llm_latency_seconds": 38.1471, "mean_llm_call_latency_seconds": 12.7157}
